      "seconds_since_start": 4.462,
      "seconds_since_previous_block": 0.067
    },
    "text": "To trace this, could you share:\n\n1. **Producer (sharing) account ID** \u2014 the account that owns the Glue database and created the Lake Formation share\n2. **Consumer account ID** \u2014 the account that can't see the database\n3. **Region** the database lives in\n4. **Database name** (and table name, if it's a specific table rather than the whole database) that was shared\n\nOnce I have those I can walk the authorization chain \u2014 Lake Formation grants, the RAM share, the resource link on the consumer side, IAM permissions, and underlying S3/KMS policies \u2014 to find where it's breaking."
  },
